1. Grant
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Subject to payment of fees and compliance with this notice, Licensor grants
Licensee a non-exclusive, non-transferable (except with Licensor consent),
worldwide license to:

  a) Use PolyRust (including core/ zero-dep pipeline and frontends) in
     binary and source form, to develop, run, and distribute Licensee's
     proprietary applications (Closed-Source Products).

  b) Run modified versions of PolyRust as a network service (SaaS, API, cloud)
     WITHOUT obligation to provide Corresponding Source under AGPL-3.0 §13.

  c) Modify core/ including unsafe_safety.rs, borrowck.rs, effects.rs,
     constraints_v2.rs, pipeline_v3.rs, but must retain safety gates unless
     otherwise agreed in writing. Removal of safety polynomials
     (1-valid)*deref=0, (1-in_unsafe)*deref=0, safe - in_unsafe*precond=0
     voids warranty and indemnity.

  d) Distribute Closed-Source Products that embed PolyRust, without licensing
     those products under AGPL-3.0.

Third-party dependencies in frontends/* (axum, tokio, syn, ureq, etc.) remain
under their own licenses (MIT/Apache-2.0). Licensee must comply with those.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Restrictions
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Licensee shall NOT:

  a) Redistribute PolyRust itself (source or binary) as a standalone product
     competing with PolyRust, without written permission.

  b) Remove or alter copyright notices, license headers, or Lean proof references
     (all_unsafe_safe_implies_no_runtime_ub, f4_ideal_invariant, etc.).

  c) Use PolyRust trademarks (PolyRust, polyrust, etc.) without written permission,
     except for "Powered by PolyRust" attribution.

  d) Sublicense PolyRust under AGPL-3.0 to third parties to circumvent commercial
     fees.

  e) Use PolyRust in safety-critical systems (e.g., avionics, automotive ASIL-D)
     without additional safety attestation and written approval. See
     pipeline_v3.rs compliance map.

