3. Fees and Support
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Fees: As per Order Form. Indicative:
    Startup (<10 employees): $2,000 / year
    SME (<100): $10,000 / year
    Enterprise: $50,000 / year + custom

  Support: Optional SLA tiers:
    - Standard: GitHub issues, 5 business day response
    - Premium: Email + Slack, 1 business day, Lean proof traceability
    - Enterprise: 24/7, on-site, custom F4/F5 tuning, audit report customization,
      QAP on-chain enterprise signing.

  Payment terms: Net 30, annual.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. Warranty and Liability (Commercial)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Unlike AGPL-3.0 §15-16 which disclaims all warranty, commercial license may
  include limited warranty as per Order Form:

  a) Licensor warrants that PolyRust as delivered will materially conform to
     documentation for 90 days.

  b) Licensor will use reasonable efforts to fix defects that cause QAP verification
     to fail or safety gates to be bypassed.

  c) EXCEPT AS EXPRESSLY PROVIDED, NO OTHER WARRANTY. IN NO EVENT SHALL LICENSOR
     BE LIABLE FOR INDIRECT, CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES BEYOND FEES PAID IN LAST 12 MONTHS.

  d) If Licensee removes safety gates (unsafe_safety.rs polynomials) or Lean
     theorems (all_unsafe_safe_implies_no_runtime_ub), warranty voids.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. Audit and Compliance
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Licensee shall:

  a) Keep audit reports (audit_report.json, qap.json, per_node_bits) for at least
     3 years.

  b) Upon Licensor request (once per year, with 30 days notice), provide
     certification of compliance and number of deployments.

  c) For ISO 26262 / IEC 61508 / DO-178C use, retain evidence of
     Lean proofs (IronLaw.lean) and Groebner basis invariance.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. Term and Termination
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Term: As per Order Form, auto-renew unless terminated.

  Termination for breach: If Licensee breaches, Licensor may terminate with
  30 days notice to cure. Upon termination, Licensee must cease use of
  PolyRust in Closed-Source Products and delete copies, except as needed for
  compliance retention.

  Termination does NOT affect AGPL-3.0 rights for versions obtained under AGPL-3.0.

